  "verbalization": "Phellandral, (R)- is linked to Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase through two distinct pathways. In the first, it acts as a target of Milatuzumab, which in turn targets Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. This suggests a direct interaction between Phellandral, (R)- and the enzyme, potentially through a mechanism involving the binding of Milatuzumab. In the second pathway, Phellandral, (R)- is linked to CDK3/Cyclin E, which is then targeted by a complex compound that ultimately affects Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. While the exact mechanism by which Phellandral, (R)- influences the enzyme remains unclear, the presence of multiple targets and the involvement of different molecular pathways indicate a complex regulatory network. The integration of these findings suggests that Phellandral, (R)- may exert its effects through a variety of molecular mechanisms, possibly involving enzyme inhibition or modulation, which could contribute to its potential therapeutic effects.",
